1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,970
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:03,240
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:05,040
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:08,310
(Episode 8)

5
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,300
Gosh. Ma'am!

6
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:01,630
Ma'am, are you okay?

7
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:04,500
Ma'am, are you okay?

8
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:06,940
I'll call 911.

9
00:01:07,070 --> 00:01:10,940
Gosh, I'm okay.
There's no need for 911.

10
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:14,110
- Oh, my.
- Are you sure you're okay?

11
00:01:16,110 --> 00:01:18,050
Here, let me help you get up.

12
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:19,550
I'll walk you home.

13
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:21,850
Oh, dear.

14
00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:38,800
It really won't light today.

15
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:47,710
Hey, Sang Beom. Long time no see.
Have you been well?

16
00:01:49,110 --> 00:01:50,110
Right.

17
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:51,950
Someone came by looking for me?

18
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:55,020
A young woman?

19
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:01,930
Goodness.

20
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:09,900
Oh, dear. Thank you.

21
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,240
You still look so pale.

22
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:15,570
Are you sure
you don't need to see a doctor?

23
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:19,480
The heat got to me,
and I felt dizzy for a second.

24
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:22,110
I'll be fine
once I get some rest at home.

25
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:27,650
It's a little warm in here.
Do you have any ice in the freezer?

26
00:02:28,750 --> 00:02:30,520
I do, but...

27
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:32,520
Stay right there.

28
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:43,540
That feels nice and cool.
I feel like I can breathe again.

29
00:02:43,870 --> 00:02:47,140
Let me do that.
I can hold it myself.

30
00:02:47,270 --> 00:02:48,270
Just try and relax.

31
00:02:48,770 --> 00:02:51,240
I just feel like
I'm imposing on you.

32
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:53,550
- It's okay.
- Goodness.

33
00:02:54,110 --> 00:02:55,380
That feels much better.

34
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,890
- Well, I should get going.
- Sure.

35
00:03:02,090 --> 00:03:04,760
Oh, speak of the devil.

36
00:03:05,790 --> 00:03:07,760
Goodness. Jung Tae, is that you?

37
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:10,800
Yes, it's Mom.

38
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:15,470
I'm doing fine, of course.

39
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:16,630
Mom.

40
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:18,870
Did anyone come by the house
looking for me?

41
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:20,810
Looking for you?

42
00:03:23,110 --> 00:03:24,880
No. Why do you ask?

43
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:26,780
Were there
any suspicious people around?

44
00:03:27,110 --> 00:03:30,080
Wait. Is something wrong?

45
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:32,050
Why do you keep asking that?

46
00:03:33,050 --> 00:03:35,090
Oh, yes. Take care now.

47
00:03:37,290 --> 00:03:38,320
Is someone at the house?

48
00:03:40,290 --> 00:03:43,230
Oh, just a young woman
who helped me.

49
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:45,960
I was grateful,
so I gave her a glass of juice.

50
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:47,230
A young woman?

51
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,400
How old is she?

52
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:52,170
What on earth is going on?

53
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,340
It's nothing.
You don't need to know.

54
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:56,570
Mom.

55
00:03:57,210 --> 00:04:00,710
From now on, don't open the door
for anyone. Got it?

56
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:04,950
Actually, on second thought...

57
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:06,820
Right.

58
00:04:08,190 --> 00:04:09,190
I see.

59
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:11,860
Is that really necessary?

60
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:18,200
All right, I hear you.

61
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:19,900
Honestly.

62
00:04:23,230 --> 00:04:25,900
You think Lee Jung Tae is
on to something?

63
00:04:26,570 --> 00:04:27,570
Yes.

64
00:04:29,170 --> 00:04:30,610
We can't let him
go deeper into hiding.

65
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:34,780
His mom said he was
in Dal-something,

66
00:04:35,010 --> 00:04:36,410
and I'm pretty sure
she meant Da Lat.

67
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:38,950
Da Lat?

68
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:40,220
Yes.

69
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:42,990
I'll keep tabs
on Lee Jung Tae's mother,

70
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:45,690
so check out
the local Korean community there.

71
00:04:46,490 --> 00:04:47,490
Sure thing.

72
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,900
By the way, Eun Seol, I'm impressed.

73
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,530
Look what you managed to figure out.

74
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:58,870
It was nothing.
I haven't even really started yet.

75
00:04:59,270 --> 00:05:01,540
Well, they do say
a good start is half the battle.

76
00:05:09,050 --> 00:05:11,050
- Hello?
- Tell me your account number.

77
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:12,450
Eun Guk?

78
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,090
Just tell me your account number.

79
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,260
Why do you need my account number?

80
00:05:18,890 --> 00:05:20,020
Do you really have to ask?

81
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:22,560
I'm sending you the money
for Mom's memorial niche,

82
00:05:22,630 --> 00:05:24,130
so give me
the account number already.

83
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,670
Seriously. Just tell me.

84
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:30,500
The account is likely frozen
due to inactivity.

85
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:32,100
If you want to give it,
do it in person.

86
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:33,470
I'm heading home right now.

87
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:39,040
Was that your brother?

88
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:41,310
Yes.

89
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:44,120
Does he still believe you're guilty?

90
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,390
I should get going.

91
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:48,950
Sure.

92
00:05:54,430 --> 00:05:55,530
Come on in.

93
00:05:56,730 --> 00:05:58,060
What brings you here?

94
00:05:58,300 --> 00:05:59,760
If you wanted to see me,
you should've called.

95
00:05:59,830 --> 00:06:01,130
I could've met you somewhere.

96
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:02,700
I'm here to see Eun Guk.

97
00:06:03,570 --> 00:06:04,570
Eun Guk?

98
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,070
Why did you come to see Eun Guk?

99
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:08,870
You know you won't hear
anything nice.

100
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:13,510
I told her to come.

101
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:17,120
Here. Take it.

102
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:19,280
What's that?

103
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:20,420
Wait.

104
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:23,390
Is it the payment
for your mom's memorial niche?

105
00:06:24,590 --> 00:06:26,190
What are you waiting for? Take it.

106
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:29,890
Why are you giving her that?
We need every penny we have.

107
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,730
Grandma, give it here.

108
00:06:32,830 --> 00:06:35,130
If she wants to ease her guilt,
let her.

109
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:36,130
Grandma!

110
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:37,700
He's right, Mom.

111
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:40,440
We should be giving this
to Eun Seol.

112
00:06:40,610 --> 00:06:43,170
She has no money
and shouldn't have to pay.

113
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:45,640
Take it, Eun Seol.

114
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,080
Let's talk.

115
00:06:51,850 --> 00:06:52,920
I have nothing to say to you.

116
00:06:54,090 --> 00:06:56,250
Do you really think I did it?

117
00:07:00,290 --> 00:07:02,390
Do you think I killed Mom?

118
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:08,130
It wasn't me, Eun Guk.

119
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:11,570
It really wasn't me.

120
00:07:12,570 --> 00:07:14,210
How could I do that?

121
00:07:15,370 --> 00:07:17,380
How could I do something like that?

122
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,980
The law found you guilty.

123
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:21,110
And I'm telling you it wasn't me!

124
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,380
Why is it so hard for you
to believe me?

125
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:28,690
Then what should I do?

126
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,990
If I killed myself right here
in front of you,

127
00:07:31,460 --> 00:07:32,690
would you believe me then?

128
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:40,130
It really wasn't me, Eun Guk.

129
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:45,170
Please, just believe me this once.

130
00:07:47,140 --> 00:07:50,140
While I'm asking nicely,
just take it and leave.

131
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:53,580
Eun Guk, seriously!

132
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:57,180
How can you do this to me?

133
00:07:57,750 --> 00:07:59,920
Even if the whole world blames me,

134
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:02,120
you of all people should believe me.

135
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:07,460
No matter what anyone else says,
at least you should believe me.

136
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:22,710
So if we cancel the new line,

137
00:08:23,010 --> 00:08:24,040
what's the alternative?

138
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,580
We'll relaunch
one of our hit products.

139
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:29,480
If we re-release our hit product...

140
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:31,580
from two years ago
in multiple colors,

141
00:08:31,650 --> 00:08:32,720
we stand a good chance of success.

142
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:33,720
However,

143
00:08:33,990 --> 00:08:35,550
the price will stay the same.

144
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:38,920
I agree with the relaunch,
but we have to raise the price.

145
00:08:39,020 --> 00:08:40,860
Right now, restoring trust
matters more than profit,

146
00:08:40,930 --> 00:08:42,390
so we should keep the price as is.

147
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:44,500
A company's primary purpose is
to generate profit.

148
00:08:44,630 --> 00:08:47,030
I believe we need
to think long-term at this point.

149
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:48,830
It's also a time
to make up for our losses.

150
00:08:48,970 --> 00:08:51,070
We just have to sell a lot of them.
More than anyone expects.

151
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:53,440
There's no guarantee
we'll sell more than expected.

152
00:08:53,670 --> 00:08:54,810
All right.

153
00:08:54,970 --> 00:08:56,540
Let's all calm down.

154
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,510
Are you sure about this?

155
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:01,380
I'm asking
if you can take responsibility.

156
00:09:02,550 --> 00:09:03,550
Yes, sir.

157
00:09:04,050 --> 00:09:05,420
If this project fails,

158
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,050
I'll take full responsibility
and resign.

159
00:09:07,490 --> 00:09:09,050
Why is that necessary?

160
00:09:09,490 --> 00:09:11,420
What does everyone else think?

161
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:14,390
I'm inclined to trust him on this.

162
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:15,860
I agree.

163
00:09:16,530 --> 00:09:19,000
Instead of focusing
on immediate profits,

164
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:21,800
I think we should look
at the long term.

165
00:09:22,870 --> 00:09:23,870
Same here.

166
00:09:24,270 --> 00:09:25,300
I agree, too.

167
00:09:27,370 --> 00:09:28,640
Excellent. In that case,

168
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:31,210
take full responsibility
and run with it.

169
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:33,140
Yes, sir.

170
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:35,610
I'll be sure to make
this project a success.

171
00:09:43,190 --> 00:09:45,320
Dad, isn't Seok Jin impressive?

172
00:09:46,990 --> 00:09:49,290
What are you trying to get at
this time?

173
00:09:49,390 --> 00:09:51,860
If he pulls off this project,
let's transfer him to HQ.

174
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:54,970
- What?
- We can't let talent like him...

175
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:56,670
waste away at a branch office.

176
00:09:57,030 --> 00:09:58,070
Let's bring him to HQ and...

177
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:59,970
There aren't any open positions.

178
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,310
We can just create one for him.

179
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:04,010
If you're just going
to talk nonsense,

180
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:05,210
get back to work.

181
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,610
But Dad...

182
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:12,180
All right.

183
00:10:28,930 --> 00:10:30,100
Welcome home, Uncle.

184
00:10:30,570 --> 00:10:32,700
Have you had dinner?
If not, go wash up and come eat.

185
00:10:35,910 --> 00:10:37,170
Enjoy your food, Teun Teun.

186
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:47,280
Is Uncle mad at you, Mom?

187
00:10:47,890 --> 00:10:48,890
Why?

188
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:51,460
- Just eat your food, Teun Teun.
- Okay.

189
00:10:58,430 --> 00:11:00,100
How long are you going
to keep this up?

190
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,470
I need to change. Get out.

191
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:06,070
What did I do that was so wrong?

192
00:11:06,570 --> 00:11:09,270
Go ask anyone else.
See if they think I was harsh.

193
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:12,380
I just thought...

194
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:14,880
you of all people
wouldn't be so prejudiced.

195
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:17,350
As if I'm some great person.

196
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:19,150
It's not because you're so great.

197
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:21,850
It's because you've suffered
from prejudice, too.

198
00:11:24,090 --> 00:11:25,990
While raising Teun Teun on your own,

199
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:28,660
you were hurt by
how people judged you.

200
00:11:29,090 --> 00:11:30,090
Am I wrong?

201
00:11:33,430 --> 00:11:36,170
I'm disappointed
I had to remind you of that.

202
00:11:52,850 --> 00:11:54,950
You're late. Have you been drinking?

203
00:11:55,350 --> 00:11:56,520
I had a drink with Assemblyman Oh.

204
00:11:58,020 --> 00:11:59,560
Mi Ran, can you make some honey tea?

205
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:00,660
Sure.

206
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,940
Tell Hae Ra
to clear her schedule this weekend.

207
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:13,870
What for?

208
00:12:14,270 --> 00:12:16,840
I've arranged for her to meet
Assemblyman Oh's second son.

209
00:12:17,410 --> 00:12:19,880
Why would you set her up
when she has Seok Jin?

210
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:22,850
Marriage isn't child's play.

211
00:12:23,050 --> 00:12:25,050
Business is all about connections,

212
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:27,320
and what better opportunity
is there than marriage?

213
00:12:28,090 --> 00:12:29,190
Don't tell me...

214
00:12:29,890 --> 00:12:32,460
Is that why you're keeping Seok Jin
in the US?

215
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:35,690
Where's my honey tea?

216
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:37,560
Hold on.

217
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,570
A blind date?

218
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:53,380
I'm already worried
because Hae Ra will refuse to go.

219
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:03,650
No way.

220
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:05,490
Why in the world would I go
on a blind date?

221
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:08,360
Going on a blind date doesn't mean
you have to get married,

222
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:10,290
so just listen to the CEO this time.

223
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,130
I said no.

224
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,800
I'm going to marry Seok Jin
no matter what,

225
00:13:14,870 --> 00:13:15,870
and that's final.

226
00:13:16,830 --> 00:13:18,940
Who said you can't marry Seok Jin?

227
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:20,100
Then what?

228
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:23,040
If the CEO keeps Seok Jin in the US,

229
00:13:23,110 --> 00:13:24,380
what will you do then?

230
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,340
He wouldn't.

231
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,780
If you stay this stubborn,

232
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:30,920
you know he's fully capable
of going that far.

233
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:35,850
Then what am I supposed to do?

234
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:38,260
First,

235
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,860
just go on the blind date
as the CEO wants...

236
00:13:40,930 --> 00:13:41,960
and buy some time.

237
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:43,930
As for Seok Jin,

238
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:46,400
I'll find a way
to bring him back to Korea.

239
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,430
How are you going to do that?

240
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:50,700
I'll figure it out.

241
00:13:54,470 --> 00:13:55,670
Let me ask you one thing.

242
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:58,610
Why do you like Seok Jin so much?

243
00:13:59,980 --> 00:14:01,610
Do you need a reason
to like someone?

244
00:14:01,610 --> 00:14:02,980
When you like someone, you just do.

245
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:06,150
Haven't you grown tired of him
after all this time?

246
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:08,890
He'd have to give me a reason first.

247
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:10,550
I wish I were tired of him.

248
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:14,060
You know...

249
00:14:14,490 --> 00:14:18,060
My whole life, I've always
gotten everything I wanted,

250
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:19,960
whether it was a person or a thing.

251
00:14:21,470 --> 00:14:24,570
But Seok Jin
has never once been mine.

252
00:14:25,570 --> 00:14:27,140
That's why I can't let him go.

253
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:29,640
Is that silly reason
all there is to it?

254
00:14:30,270 --> 00:14:32,940
It's not silly.
To me, it's everything.

255
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:37,250
All right. Get some rest.

256
00:14:49,130 --> 00:14:50,130
Hello?

257
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:52,560
Sorry, I'm in a meeting.
I'll call later.

258
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:53,630
Seok Jin, wait!

259
00:14:56,930 --> 00:14:58,440
How can I get tired of him
when he's like this?

260
00:15:07,210 --> 00:15:08,580
Do you think this relaunch...

261
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:10,680
will cover the losses
from the new product?

262
00:15:12,050 --> 00:15:13,050
That's a good point.

263
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:17,250
We have to raise prices
because of inflation.

264
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:21,130
We're freezing the prices.

265
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:23,990
Instead,

266
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:25,230
we'll introduce pre-orders...

267
00:15:25,230 --> 00:15:27,770
and the Drop Method
both online and offline.

268
00:15:28,730 --> 00:15:31,270
But pre-orders will lead
to shipping delays.

269
00:15:31,870 --> 00:15:33,400
We're turning the wait
into part of its value.

270
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,670
Then what about the Drop Method?

271
00:15:35,870 --> 00:15:37,710
Buy now or miss out forever.

272
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:39,410
You're triggering that mindset.

273
00:15:39,510 --> 00:15:40,910
Once that scarcity factor kicks in,

274
00:15:40,980 --> 00:15:42,810
we won't have to spend
a single dollar on marketing...

275
00:15:42,950 --> 00:15:45,320
because customers will flock
to our site on their own.

276
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,990
Then the money we save on ads
becomes pure profit.

277
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,120
Exactly.

278
00:15:50,550 --> 00:15:52,490
Hire some celebrities
and run a campaign.

279
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:55,730
That while trends change,
Cheongma's value is timeless.

280
00:15:56,430 --> 00:15:58,360
A brilliant plan, as expected
from our branch manager.

281
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:00,530
I'll get on it right away. Let's go.

282
00:16:09,910 --> 00:16:11,180
You wanted to see me, Ms. Joo?

283
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:13,380
Dig up some dirt on Chief Choi.

284
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:15,650
You mean Chief Choi
from the Planning Department?

285
00:16:16,050 --> 00:16:17,050
May I ask why?

286
00:16:17,050 --> 00:16:18,820
I need his position cleared out.

287
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:21,390
Oh, so you want to...

288
00:16:22,390 --> 00:16:24,490
It isn't for me,
it's for Cha Seok Jin.

289
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:26,560
Cha Seok Jin? What for?

290
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:29,090
Because bringing him back
to help Hae Ra...

291
00:16:29,090 --> 00:16:30,360
is how I can help myself.

292
00:16:32,530 --> 00:16:33,860
There's bound to be...

293
00:16:33,930 --> 00:16:35,970
some shady business
behind the upcoming event.

294
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:39,670
Go see if Chief Choi has
a deal going with the agency.

295
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:41,540
Yes, ma'am.

296
00:16:53,350 --> 00:16:55,020
Why do you keep calling me?

297
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:56,650
I already told you I'd pay you back.

298
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:01,960
It's just that my stocks
and crypto are tied up right now,

299
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:03,560
so please be patient.

300
00:17:05,630 --> 00:17:07,660
If I have to,
I'll even sell my house.

301
00:17:10,230 --> 00:17:11,870
This is driving me crazy.

302
00:17:12,470 --> 00:17:14,710
Look at the mess
Director Joo put me in.

303
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:18,380
The stress is killing me.

304
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,380
There's no one home.

305
00:17:53,810 --> 00:17:56,410
But an elderly woman lives here.

306
00:17:57,950 --> 00:17:59,920
You must mean Jung Tae's mother.

307
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,590
She left the other day
to visit her younger sibling.

308
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,520
Her younger sibling?

309
00:18:05,790 --> 00:18:08,130
Do you have any idea
when she'll be back?

310
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:12,200
When she left, she said
she'd be gone for a while.

311
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:17,270
By the way, who are you?
Why are you looking for her?

312
00:18:18,470 --> 00:18:21,140
- Do you have the address?
- Oh, please.

313
00:18:21,670 --> 00:18:23,610
How would I know that?

314
00:18:33,350 --> 00:18:35,250
Lee Jung Tae's mother
has disappeared?

315
00:18:37,390 --> 00:18:39,560
All right.
I'll look into it further.

316
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:52,940
(Da Lat Korean Community, Vietnam)

317
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:56,140
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

318
00:19:04,650 --> 00:19:06,680
Ms. Joo, it's just as you suspected.

319
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:09,220
Chief Choi received kickbacks
from the agency.

320
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:11,960
He inflated the event costs
and received a portion back.

321
00:19:13,390 --> 00:19:15,390
- How much?
- Thirty percent.

322
00:19:17,230 --> 00:19:18,660
That's quite a lot.

323
00:19:19,060 --> 00:19:20,130
So greedy.

324
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:23,300
What should I do now?
Should I report it?

325
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:25,740
Manager Na, keep your name off it.

326
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,240
Just send an anonymous tip to Legal.

327
00:19:28,570 --> 00:19:29,970
Let them handle it from there.

328
00:19:31,110 --> 00:19:32,580
Yes, I understand.

329
00:19:32,610 --> 00:19:34,280
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

330
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:42,120
Now I won't have to see
that irritating face anymore.

331
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:45,420
Come in.

332
00:19:50,130 --> 00:19:51,190
What is it?

333
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:54,130
An anonymous tip was just sent
to the Legal Team's email.

334
00:19:55,730 --> 00:19:58,170
An anonymous tip? What is it about?

335
00:19:58,540 --> 00:19:59,970
It says Chief Choi from Planning...

336
00:19:59,970 --> 00:20:02,270
has been taking a cut
through kickbacks.

337
00:20:03,970 --> 00:20:05,640
Are you sure the source is reliable?

338
00:20:06,410 --> 00:20:08,280
The information provided
is quite specific.

339
00:20:08,550 --> 00:20:10,550
There's even some evidence attached.

340
00:20:14,050 --> 00:20:15,390
Then let's head
to the Planning Team first...

341
00:20:15,390 --> 00:20:16,790
and secure all related documents.

342
00:20:16,990 --> 00:20:17,990
Let's go.

343
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:25,030
Chief Choi, are you
out of your mind?

344
00:20:25,330 --> 00:20:26,700
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

345
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:27,970
I have no excuse for my actions.

346
00:20:28,330 --> 00:20:29,830
Please, just forgive me
this one time.

347
00:20:31,130 --> 00:20:32,140
Forgive you?

348
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:33,770
If you just look the other way
this one time,

349
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:35,870
I'll devote my life to serving you.

350
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:37,870
Don't you get it? It's too late.

351
00:20:38,110 --> 00:20:39,910
The entire company
already knows everything,

352
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:42,210
so me turning a blind eye
won't solve anything.

353
00:20:43,180 --> 00:20:45,020
Are you telling me to just quit?

354
00:20:45,150 --> 00:20:47,920
Chief Choi, your job
is the least of your worries.

355
00:20:48,090 --> 00:20:50,550
The Legal Team has already filed
a criminal complaint.

356
00:20:50,950 --> 00:20:52,660
A criminal complaint?

357
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:54,930
Just leave.

358
00:20:55,590 --> 00:20:57,830
- Sir...
- I said, leave.

359
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,570
You really can't trust anyone
these days.

360
00:21:09,770 --> 00:21:11,910
Who'd have thought Chief Choi
would do such a thing?

361
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:15,810
I know. The CEO must be devastated.

362
00:21:16,110 --> 00:21:19,020
Of course he is.
He just lost his right-hand man.

363
00:21:19,750 --> 00:21:21,550
- Unbelievable.
- Mom.

364
00:21:24,220 --> 00:21:25,590
Did you hear about Chief Choi?

365
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:28,360
We were just talking about him.

366
00:21:28,590 --> 00:21:31,130
I knew he was like that
from the very beginning.

367
00:21:31,530 --> 00:21:33,030
It's so satisfying.

368
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:35,100
This must be what it feels like
to finally pull a bad tooth.

369
00:21:36,630 --> 00:21:38,640
Your father's home.
Be careful what you say.

370
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:41,970
Hey, you're home.

371
00:21:41,970 --> 00:21:43,010
Right.

372
00:21:43,070 --> 00:21:44,310
Hey, Dad.

373
00:21:44,740 --> 00:21:46,110
I'll just head inside.

374
00:21:56,690 --> 00:21:58,260
Nice one, Ms. Joo.

375
00:21:59,590 --> 00:22:00,820
What are you talking about?

376
00:22:01,020 --> 00:22:02,460
Stop playing dumb.

377
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:04,900
I know you pulled all this
just to make room for Seok Jin.

378
00:22:06,130 --> 00:22:09,500
Out of curiosity, do you really
want me to marry Seok Jin?

379
00:22:10,570 --> 00:22:11,870
Why do you ask?

380
00:22:14,440 --> 00:22:15,840
I was just suddenly curious.

381
00:22:16,810 --> 00:22:20,140
I thought you weren't a fan
of guys like Seok Jin.

382
00:22:21,450 --> 00:22:25,080
I just want you to inherit Cheongma.

383
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:28,320
By the looks of it,
you can't manage on your own.

384
00:22:28,890 --> 00:22:31,090
And Seok Jin seemed like
he'd be a great help.

385
00:22:32,620 --> 00:22:34,120
Does that answer your question?

386
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:35,460
Completely.

387
00:22:36,690 --> 00:22:40,030
Regardless, you're dangerous
to have as an enemy.

388
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,770
It's not over yet.
So don't go popping the champagne.

389
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:45,470
What do you mean by that?

390
00:22:46,670 --> 00:22:47,870
Just because there's an opening...

391
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:49,970
doesn't mean it's Seok Jin's
for the taking.

392
00:22:50,570 --> 00:22:52,110
The CEO has to give his approval.

393
00:22:53,210 --> 00:22:56,480
That's true. My dad can't stand him.

394
00:22:56,750 --> 00:22:58,120
How can we get Dad to approve?

395
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,130
Branch Manager Cha.

396
00:23:13,500 --> 00:23:16,930
The scarcity strategy
was a total success.

397
00:23:18,700 --> 00:23:22,170
Yesterday, the server even crashed
from all the traffic.

398
00:23:22,170 --> 00:23:23,970
Was it restored quickly?

399
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:27,610
Oh, of course.
Try to enjoy it a little, okay?

400
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:31,450
All right.

401
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:34,380
You two really put in the work.

402
00:23:34,820 --> 00:23:35,820
Cheers.

403
00:23:40,290 --> 00:23:41,320
Mr. Cha,

404
00:23:41,930 --> 00:23:43,130
since this project
was such a massive hit,

405
00:23:43,190 --> 00:23:44,830
don't you think
they'll bring you back to HQ?

406
00:23:44,830 --> 00:23:47,630
I heard the Planning Chief position
is currently open.

407
00:23:48,430 --> 00:23:49,670
I'm not that interested.

408
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:52,070
Come on. As if.

409
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:56,240
It's the CEO.

410
00:23:57,570 --> 00:23:59,040
Here comes the promotion.

411
00:24:02,780 --> 00:24:05,150
- Yes, sir.
- Great work.

412
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:07,120
Thank you.

413
00:24:07,220 --> 00:24:09,120
I'm sending a special bonus
for your team's success,

414
00:24:09,420 --> 00:24:11,120
so congratulate the staff for me.

415
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:13,660
I see. Of course.

416
00:24:14,990 --> 00:24:16,790
I'll see you
next time I'm in the US.

417
00:24:17,090 --> 00:24:18,400
Yes, sir. Thank you.

418
00:24:26,100 --> 00:24:28,640
What? Why did you hang up already?

419
00:24:30,870 --> 00:24:31,880
Oh, that.

420
00:24:32,310 --> 00:24:34,410
The CEO is giving us
a special bonus,

421
00:24:34,740 --> 00:24:36,650
so pick a nice place
for our team dinner.

422
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:38,950
I see. Understood.

423
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:41,690
Let's have a drink. Come on.

424
00:24:41,690 --> 00:24:42,690
Right.

425
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:51,360
The Chief of Planning position.

426
00:24:51,830 --> 00:24:53,830
I don't know how long
we can leave it vacant.

427
00:24:54,030 --> 00:24:55,530
This is a real problem.

428
00:24:57,500 --> 00:24:59,440
I'm sure my husband will handle it.

429
00:25:02,310 --> 00:25:04,210
What about Cha Seok Jin?

430
00:25:04,210 --> 00:25:05,340
Seok Jin?

431
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:10,210
For Hae Ra's sake,
I'd like that too, but...

432
00:25:11,010 --> 00:25:12,680
My husband wouldn't agree to it.

433
00:25:13,320 --> 00:25:15,920
The company's in a crisis.
At a time like this,

434
00:25:16,020 --> 00:25:18,190
don't we need someone we can trust?

435
00:25:19,960 --> 00:25:21,290
That's true, but...

436
00:25:22,930 --> 00:25:26,230
Ma'am, perhaps you should make
a real effort to convince him.

437
00:25:27,260 --> 00:25:29,770
The CEO was just betrayed
by Chief Choi,

438
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:31,970
so he must be feeling vulnerable.

439
00:25:33,340 --> 00:25:35,410
You're right, Director Joo.

440
00:25:37,170 --> 00:25:39,110
I'll try to persuade him.

441
00:25:48,550 --> 00:25:51,620
You're going to hire an outsider
for the Chief of Planning position?

442
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:54,460
Yes, I've been looking
at candidates.

443
00:25:55,430 --> 00:25:58,760
Why is that necessary?
Just bring Seok Jin in.

444
00:25:59,430 --> 00:26:00,600
That's not happening.

445
00:26:00,760 --> 00:26:03,230
Why not?
He just pulled off a major success.

446
00:26:03,500 --> 00:26:06,870
I told you, I have no intention
of having Seok Jin as my son-in-law.

447
00:26:06,900 --> 00:26:08,870
We can worry about that later.

448
00:26:08,870 --> 00:26:10,970
Don't you realize
the company is in a crisis?

449
00:26:11,410 --> 00:26:13,340
When even your right-hand man
has betrayed you,

450
00:26:13,610 --> 00:26:15,650
how can you trust an outsider
with that position?

451
00:26:16,180 --> 00:26:18,110
I'll just have to keep
a close eye on them.

452
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:20,750
Did Chief Choi betray you
because you let your guard down?

453
00:26:23,590 --> 00:26:24,750
No matter how I look at it,

454
00:26:24,820 --> 00:26:26,860
there's no better person
for the job than Seok Jin,

455
00:26:27,090 --> 00:26:28,660
so just do as I say this time.

456
00:26:30,290 --> 00:26:31,800
Honey, hold on. That's...

457
00:26:35,570 --> 00:26:36,570
My gosh.

458
00:26:37,270 --> 00:26:39,940
I can't believe
you were eavesdropping.

459
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:41,500
That was great, Mom.

460
00:26:42,070 --> 00:26:44,810
You're the only one
who really gets me.

461
00:26:45,380 --> 00:26:46,480
Honestly.

462
00:26:47,340 --> 00:26:49,150
It's not just for your sake.

463
00:26:49,710 --> 00:26:52,550
I actually think Seok Jin
is the right person for the job.

464
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:55,690
Anyway, let me give you a massage
to thank you.

465
00:26:55,750 --> 00:26:56,950
- Come here, Mom.
- Goodness.

466
00:26:58,120 --> 00:27:01,060
Look at you, acting
so out of character. Honestly.

467
00:27:02,130 --> 00:27:03,790
- My gosh.
- Does that feel good?

468
00:27:04,890 --> 00:27:05,900
(Da Lat Korean Community)

469
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:08,670
(Good finds, Good Vibes
in Da Lat)

470
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:13,900
There you are.

471
00:27:23,980 --> 00:27:25,380
(Let's get barbecue
for our next get-together.)

472
00:27:30,090 --> 00:27:31,090
You found him?

473
00:27:31,250 --> 00:27:35,060
Yes. I just sent a photo
to your email, so take a look.

474
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:36,560
One moment.

475
00:27:39,430 --> 00:27:41,660
(Eun Seol, I've confirmed
Lee Jung Tae's whereabouts.)

476
00:27:43,430 --> 00:27:44,530
It's him. It's Lee Jung Tae.

477
00:27:46,740 --> 00:27:49,340
Then do you know his address
in Vietnam by any chance?

478
00:27:50,470 --> 00:27:53,240
Why?
Are you planning to go to Vietnam?

479
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:56,450
I have to.
It's the only way I can meet him.

480
00:27:57,180 --> 00:27:58,420
That won't be necessary.

481
00:27:58,820 --> 00:28:00,120
Our hunch was right.

482
00:28:00,780 --> 00:28:03,120
Lee Jung Tae is coming
to Korea next week.

483
00:28:03,620 --> 00:28:04,720
Next week?

484
00:28:05,190 --> 00:28:06,860
Check the comments
in the link I sent you.

485
00:28:11,900 --> 00:28:13,060
(Lee's post)

486
00:28:13,060 --> 00:28:15,730
Jung Tae, you're going
to Korea next week?

487
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:17,000
Have a great time.

488
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:19,040
I want to go to Korea too.

489
00:28:20,700 --> 00:28:22,070
So he's coming on his own accord?

490
00:28:23,270 --> 00:28:25,440
He has to be coming
to meet whoever hired him.

491
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:27,280
That must be it.

492
00:28:28,650 --> 00:28:29,880
Thank you, Attorney Seo.

493
00:28:30,810 --> 00:28:32,280
Come on. Don't mention it.

494
00:28:33,150 --> 00:28:35,690
I want to catch the real killer
just as much as you do.

495
00:28:36,950 --> 00:28:39,290
This time, we'll catch them.

496
00:28:39,890 --> 00:28:40,920
We'll get the real killer...

497
00:28:41,660 --> 00:28:43,460
and clear your name.

498
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:45,960
Then my mission will be complete.

499
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:49,330
Yes. Let's do that.

500
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:25,470
Mr. Seok Jin, I really have to go.

501
00:29:25,900 --> 00:29:26,970
To the restroom?

502
00:29:26,970 --> 00:29:27,970
Yes.

503
00:29:30,470 --> 00:29:31,570
There's one over there.

504
00:29:32,040 --> 00:29:33,140
Can you go by yourself?

505
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:35,250
Yes, I can go by myself.

506
00:29:35,850 --> 00:29:36,850
Can you keep an eye on this?

507
00:31:30,430 --> 00:31:34,130
(A Trap Called Desire)

508
00:31:34,430 --> 00:31:36,730
- My daughter-in-law?
- She's the one I'm going to marry.

509
00:31:37,100 --> 00:31:38,800
Congratulations on your promotion,
Chief Cha.

510
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:41,400
I just thought you should know
that I have your back.

511
00:31:41,470 --> 00:31:44,140
It's only a matter of time
before Ko Eun Seol finds me.

512
00:31:44,210 --> 00:31:46,110
Or maybe I could just go to her.

513
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:48,040
Should I have the guys
take care of him?

514
00:31:48,110 --> 00:31:49,180
What does he want?

515
00:31:49,250 --> 00:31:51,610
We need to look into it
since it's our only clue.

516
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:52,750
Leave it to me.

517
00:31:52,920 --> 00:31:54,980
So what are you going to do now?

518
00:31:55,220 --> 00:31:57,120
I'm going to find the person
who hurt Mom...

519
00:31:57,250 --> 00:31:58,590
and make them pay.

520
00:31:58,590 --> 00:31:59,760
Cheongma Group?

521
00:32:00,260 --> 00:32:03,760
So, will we find out who hired
Lee Jung Tae by tomorrow?

522
00:32:05,830 --> 00:32:07,830
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
